	)
	(text "Solar Input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.59 52.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.048 3.048)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ecb8301e-2ff2-45f1-9b5b-9f83ffa7e677")
	)
	(text_box "SOLAR INPUT - 4 face PCBs (X+, X-, Y+, Y-), each with 4x SM141K10TF in series (~\n8.4V Vmp, ~~23.6V Voc, ~~41mA Imp per face).  Faces are paralleled through blocking diodes on this board.  Realistic orbit current: 40-80mA depending on attitude.  Bench supply can simulate any condition through any single JST connector."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 125.73 54.61 0)
		(size -101.6 20.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5643e3b1-9607-4c82-a49d-8180e6c4d946")
	)
	(text_box "Cell count = 2S Li-Ion: CELLS1 =- INTVCC, CELLS0 = VCC2P5.  Matches DC2038A demo board jumper configuration for 2-cell Li-Ion.  Full charge voltage = 2 x 4.2 = 8.4V. See LTC4162-L datasheet Table 5 (p.48) and DC2038A Table 1 (p.5)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.039 122.599 0)
		(size -43.689 20.911)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7473cd1e-6818-4d60-a426-ab269e490d88")
	)
	(text_box "@{\"Id\":\"NFZYWHM~{E}PGCWUXVN\",\"ObjectType\":2} Input reverse-blocking MOSFET.  LTC4162 gives gate via INFET charge pump.  FDMC8327L selected per DC2038A reference design.\n@{\"Id\":\"NFZYWHM~{E}MTBRIUZQ\",\"ObjectType\":2} Input current sense.  I_IN(MAX) = 32nV / 10mOhm = 3.2A.  Sized for bench supply flexibility -- actual solar panels deliver only ~~80mA.  Use Kelvin connection (4-pad footprint preferred, sense traces from inner pads to CLP/CLN pins).  See LTC4162-L datasheet Figure 5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 339.09 24.13 0)
		(size -93.98 15.24)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b66b6fb0-7ba1-4d76-a4cd-1a9b0aa3c5e1")
	)
	(text_box "Solar panel impedance compensation per LTC4263-L datasheet Fig. 8. 2.5 Ohm + 150uF maintains ~~2.5 Ohm real impedance in the 1-10KHz band where the MPPT loop operates.  Required for panels with high dynamic impedance in the constant-current region.  The 150uF should be solid polymer or aluminum-polymer (not wet electrolytic) for stable ESR over temperature.  Panasonic ZA hybrid series recommended."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 59.69 143.51 0)
		(size -35.56 38.1)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e9b9aa3c-12f2-4473-8a03-c5845dc9f424")
	)
	(text_box "I2C address: 0x68 (7-bit). Up to 400kHz (Fast Mode).  DVCC = INTVCC (~~5V) sets I2C logic levels.  The flight controller must be 5V-tolerant on I2C or use a level shifter.  If FC runs at 3.3V I2C, either: \n(a): connect DVCC to 3.3V instead of INTVCC (works per datasheet if DVCC >=2.667V), or\n(b): add a bidirectional I2C level shifter.  Decision TBD during integration -- for now, wire DVCC to INTVCC and note the open item."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 168.91 54.61 0)
		(size -35.56 38.1)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fd0b00f4-03ec-4b7f-b4dd-9c58dc96e48f")
	)
